My understanding is that Nethack either requires significant scratch
space or ram.  The GBA has neither.

That being said, someone has already ported Hack to the GBA:
http://www.freewebs.com/drussell/Download.htm

Personally, I feel that the ergonomics of the game boy advance are
sufficiently different from those of a PC (considerably lower
resolution, extremely few buttons, etc) that porting Nethack would not
result in the most fun playing experience.  That's why when I wanted
to play a roguelike on the GBA, I started from scratch.  It's been a
year, so while it is not near Nethack in complexity, it is, IMHO,
quite playable.

I am heavily influenced from Nethack, so those used to Nethack's style
would likely find it similar:

